    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that's a bit vague lol. when you say \"consensus,\" do you mean most economists actually agree the growth was worth the inequality, or is it still a 50/50 split? i'm seeing a lot of scholars saying the deregulation was basically the main driver for the massive wealth gap we see today. is that considered a mainstream view or just one side of the debate?",
